## Adjudication Summary

I evaluated all four Wave A analyses against the five Wave B critiques. The consensus is clear and I am ruling as follows:

Valid criticisms (incorporated):
- Preserve every original test token — layer gradients over `bg-primary/bg-destructive/bg-secondary`, keep `border`, `hover:bg-accent`, `text-primary`, `rounded-md`. This eliminates all existing-test breakage. (REGRESSION_HUNTER, DEPENDENCY_AUDITOR, ADVERSARIAL_CRITIC)
- Reject INDEPENDENT_STRATEGIST's approach of rewriting existing assertions. Disqualifying — original tests must pass untouched.
- `transition-all` → scoped `transition-[transform,box-shadow,background-color,border-color]` to avoid layout thrash and framer-motion contention. (SCALE_REVIEWER, REGRESSION_HUNTER)
- Remove `will-change-transform` from the base — per-instance compositor promotion is a GPU hazard in dense grids. (SCALE_REVIEWER)
- Restore `disabled:opacity-50` — dropping to `opacity-40` is a WCAG perceivability regression. (UI_UX_POLISH)
- Use literal hex `ring-[#00E096]`, not `[color:var(--brand)]` (Tailwind version portability), and drop the explicit `ring-offset` color to avoid the mismatched-halo problem inside raised cards. (DEPENDENCY_AUDITOR, UI_UX_POLISH)
- Keep `rounded-md` (reject Proposal 2's `rounded-lg` global radius regression).
- `index.css`: strip the global `!important` reduced-motion / global `button {}` transition rules. Component-level `motion-reduce:*` utilities are authoritative; the appended block is minimal and non-animating only.
- Ghost/link stay flat (no transform) — correct emphasis hierarchy.

Noise (rejected):
- Bundle-size hand-wringing over ~20 arbitrary utilities — negligible, static strings, JIT-scanned. No action.
- "Hex assertions are brittle" — true in theory, but mechanical `toHaveClass` checks are the deterministic contract here; I assert structural tokens (`bg-gradient-to-b`, `hover:-translate-y-px`) plus token fallbacks, minimizing hex coupling.

Note: original `button.test.jsx` never asserted `focus-visible:ring-ring`, `transition-colors`, or `disabled:opacity-50`, so no existing assertion changes. I only add coverage.

